@startuml cli-google-books-import
' Where each memory/reliability flag of `train import-google-books` acts.
' The import is a two-stage pipeline: a DOWNLOAD path (HTTP or local .gz) and a
' WRITE path (parse -> lock-free overlay -> chunked transaction -> shard
' checkpoint + eviction -> merge). --cache-files bounds the download path;
' --tx-chunk-size, --lockfree-flush-threshold and --overlay-budget-gib each bound
' a distinct buffer on the write path. Flag callouts are notes on the exact stage
' they govern.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/cli-google-books-import.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/cli/import-google-books.md §3.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #ECEFF1
  BorderColor #546E7A
  FontColor #263238
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title train import-google-books — which flag bounds which buffer

rectangle "**Google Books n-gram files**\n.gz, one per (order × prefix)" as src #455A64
rectangle "**Download workers**\n""--parallel"" (default 4)" as dl #546E7A
rectangle "**Local cache**\n{output_dir}/grammstein-cache/" as cache #546E7A
rectangle "**Local files**\n""--local-files <DIR>""" as local #546E7A

rectangle "**Parser + filters**\nrecord ⟶ (n-gram, year, count)\n""--min-count"" · ""--min-year"" / ""--max-year""\n""--skip-pos-tags"" · ""--prefix""" as parse #1565C0
rectangle "**Lock-free overlay**\nper-shard concurrent write buffer" as overlay #1565C0
rectangle "**Chunked transaction**\nbuffer entries, then commit" as tx #00838F
rectangle "**Shard checkpoint + eviction**\ncoldest resident overlay nodes evicted\n(lossless — they fault back on read)" as ckpt #00838F
rectangle "**Merge**\nshards ⟶ PersistentARTrie\n""--sharding"" · ""--keep-shards""" as merge #00838F
rectangle "**OUTPUT**\npositional argument" as out #455A64

src --> dl : HTTP
dl --> cache : ""--cache-files""
cache --> parse
dl --> parse : streamed\n(default)
local --> parse
src ..> local : pre-downloaded\nby the operator

parse --> overlay
overlay --> tx : flush
tx --> ckpt : commit
ckpt --> merge
merge --> out

note right of cache
  ""--cache-files"" (default: off)
  Download each .gz to disk first, then parse
  from the local file. Survives a mid-stream
  network blip; costs local disk.
end note

note right of overlay
  ""--lockfree-flush-threshold <ENTRIES>""
  Auto: 50 000 when ""--parallel"" ≥ 8, else
  100 000. Caps **inter-checkpoint** overlay growth.
end note

note right of tx
  ""--tx-chunk-size <ENTRIES>"" (default 500 000)
  Entries buffered per transaction.
  0 disables chunking (whole file in one tx).
end note

note right of ckpt
  ""--overlay-budget-gib <GIB>"" (default 10)
  Global **post-checkpoint resident** overlay
  budget, divided across resident shards.
  0 disables eviction.
end note

@enduml
